  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Catholic Secretariat of Nigeria (CSN)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant to the Catholic Secretariat of Nigeria forms part of the Programme &#x201c;Improving Primary Health Care for Rural Poor Communities in Northern Nigeria&#x201d;, and focuses on the fourth objective of the Programme: &#x201c;To build the capacity of the Catholic Church in health policy and advocacy issues to influence the development and monitoring of pro-poor health policies.&#x201d;

There is a widely held recognition in Nigeria that in order to influence the development of pro-poor health policies that ensure equal access to health services, it is first necessary to strengthen the advocacy and lobbying skills of non-state actors (NSAs).  As part of the project, a Health Policy &amp; Advocacy Adviser has been recruited to help establish a Health Advocacy Unit within CSN to advocate for pro-poor health policies in Nigeria and ensure greater coordination and networking among sector actors.  The Health Policy &amp; Advocacy Adviser will provide training to key personnel/advocacy champions within the Catholic Secretariat and Catholic health services and, in consultation with other actors, to develop a CSN advocacy strategy.  The Health Advocacy Unit will also identify advocacy champions from 3 focal pilot states within the geographical area covered by the Programme.  The &#x2018;champions&#x2019; will be representative of all layers including government, civil society organisations and communities.</narrative>
  </description>
